      "text": "shall a man leave his father, Gen. 2:24 (Matt. 19:5; Mark 10:7; Eph. 5:31; Moses 3:24; Abr. 5:18). he left his garment in her hand, and fled, Gen. 39:12. Entreat me not to leave thee, Ruth 1:16. I only, am left, 1 Kgs. 19:10 (Rom. 11:3). wilt not leave my soul in hell, Ps. 16:10 (Acts 2:27). leave me not, neither forsake me, O God, Ps. 27:9. he that is left in Zion … shall be called holy, Isa. 4:3 (2 Ne. 14:3). two parts … cut off and die; but the third shall be left, Zech. 13:8. day that cometh … shall leave them neither root nor branch, Mal. 4:1 (3 Ne. 25:1; D&C 133:64; JS—H 1:37).",
