      "text": "devil leaveth him … angels came and ministered, Matt. 4:11. Leave there thy gift before the altar, Matt. 5:24. that was left seven baskets full, Matt. 15:37 (Mark 8:8). doth he not leave the ninety and nine, Matt. 18:12 (Luke 15:4). not to leave the other undone, Matt. 23:23 (Luke 11:42). shall not be left here one stone, Matt. 24:2 (Mark 13:2; Luke 21:6; D&C 45:20; JS—M 1:3). one shall be taken, and the other left, Matt. 24:40 (JS—M 1:44). we have left all, and have followed, Mark 10:28 (Luke 18:28). he left all, rose up, and followed him, Luke 5:28. hireling … seeth the wolf coming, and leaveth the sheep, John 10:12. I will not leave you comfortless, John 14:18. I leave the world, and go to the Father, John 16:28. husband … let her not leave him, 1 Cor. 7:13. leaving the principles of the doctrine of Christ, Heb. 6:1. I will never leave thee, nor forsake thee, Heb. 13:5. because thou hast left thy first love, Rev. 2:4.",
